The Opportunity


Join our Acceleration Center India and help shape the future of business for our diverse client portfolio across geographies and jurisdictions. You’ll work at the heart of global teams across Advisory, Assurance, Tax and Business Services—solving real client challenges through connected collaboration. We’ll help you grow your skills so you can go further. With hands-on learning, cutting-edge tools and an inclusive culture, this is your opportunity to do inspiring work that makes a difference—every day.


As a Strategy& Value Creation - Working Capital - Senior Associate you will support deal strategy work focused on working capital analysis, value creation opportunities, and transaction support for clients across the deal lifecycle within our Deals practice. As a Senior Associate you will analyze complex issues, manage assigned workstreams, build client relationships, and guide junior team members while applying professional judgment and technical skills to deliver clear, decision-useful insights. In this role at PwC, you will contribute to transaction diligence, interpret financial and operational data, identify working capital drivers, and help shape deliverables that support clients as they pursue value creation across acquisitions, divestitures, and broader strategic initiatives.


**Responsibilities**

* Assess a company’s working capital performance leveraging their balance sheet and P&L to calculate working capital KPIs
* Benchmark a company against competitors using public and proprietary information, using the output to draw conclusions on a company’s relative performance;
* Conduct analytics on ‘transactional data’ such as customer / supplier invoices, POs / Sales Orders, goods receipt / issues, material movement data and working capital financing to identify data insights on root cause drivers of working capital using analytical tools;
* Understand key business processes and support internal stakeholders to facilitate sessions on key processes driving working capital with clients to identify opportunities, such as setting contractual terms, collections, procurement, purchasing and supply chain
* Perform financial analysis of opportunities for working capital reduction, within the context of commercial requirements of the business;
* Conduct assessment of operational and management teams within an organisation, identifying skill gaps and training needs;
* Manage the end-to-end delivery of project work packages, delivering time-critical services to satisfy client deadlines;
* Identify and assess risks which could affect project delivery, proactively highlighting them to key stakeholders;
* and
* Be responsible for internal initiatives of the Business Unit and contribute to our culture of continuous improvement, including the upskilling of other team members.

What You Must Have



* 4 years of previous experience in Supply Chain, Credit Management/Receivables and Procurement roles, or Working Capital consulting experience in the UK or continental Europe;
* Experience in engagements to improve supply chain management, procurement, buying, collections management, inventory reduction or general working capital optimisation;
* Good end-to-end understanding of flows of goods and services, information and money and how different functions cooperate internally and externally;
* Sound financial analysis skills (collecting, manipulating and analysing financial and non-financial data), including strong use of Microsoft Excel;
* Strong commercial awareness and business analysis skills;
* A solid understanding of operational business drivers and critical thinking to enable the "So what" analysis;
* A solid understanding of the components of working capital and influencing levers;
* Report writing skills, including use of Microsoft PowerPoint;
* Strong interpersonal, presentation & excellent communication skills (Oral and Written to a high business English standard);
* Strong project management, organisational and project delivery skills;
* Demonstrated experience utilising analytics and visualisation tools including but not limited to Alteryx, Tableau and Power BI (any certifications would be preferable e.g. Alteryx Core and Alteryx Advanced);
* Ability to multi-task and communicate effectively across teams in a high-performance culture;
* Ability to work effectively in a globally dispersed team environment; and
* Working knowledge and understanding of current AI technology tools would be preferable.

**TITLE: Associate, Asset Management Brio India**
**DEPARTMENT:**
**Brio Asset Management**
**REPORTS TO: VP, Asset Management Brio India**
In 2025, Blackstone established Brio Real Estate (“Brio”) as a portfolio company focused on real estate credit. Brio is a specialized global commercial real estate asset services platform that manages and supports Blackstone’s Real Estate Debt Strategies business (“BREDS”) across the globe. Today, BREDS has more than $77 billion in investor capital across high yield / opportunistic real estate credit funds, a publicly traded Mortgage REIT, CMBS securities and insurance capital. Brio is a sophisticated real estate credit solutions provider that enhances value for investors and supports BREDS across key functions, including asset management, transactions, capital markets, surveillance, portfolio management and legal & compliance. Brio provides critical infrastructure and capabilities for BREDS to allow for effective investments and management of its global portfolio.


Blackstone is the world’s largest alternative asset manager with more than $1 trillion in assets under management. Blackstone’s scale, with roughly 12,700 real estate assets and over 240 portfolio companies, enables them to invest in dynamic sectors positioned for long-term growth. The firm seeks to deliver compelling returns for institutional and individual investors by building strong businesses that deliver lasting value. Blackstone’s global investment strategies focus on real estate, private equity, infrastructure, life sciences, growth equity, credit, secondaries and hedge funds.


**Job Summary**

* Execute asset management strategies to ensure sound management and risk mitigation across the global commercial real estate debt portfolio;
* Oversee the performance of all commercial real estate debt assets including assisting with monitoring loan performance, covenant compliance, capex tracking, IPD waterfall analysis, redemptions, prepayments, disposals, asset-level business plans, lease-up progress, borrower financials, quarterly loan reviews and on-going portfolio management workstreams;
* Produce portfolio-wide analytics to support strategic decision-making and identify emerging trends
* Operate with clear, consistent communication and expectation‑setting across a wide range of internal and external stakeholders, including Borrowers, Sponsors, syndicate/participant Lenders, Servicers, and other counterparties;
* Coordinating with lenders, borrowers and their respective lawyers in respect to loan redemptions, restructuring, amendments, waivers and other ad hoc requests.
* Provide competent analysis of a portfolio of loans and underlying security on a quarterly basis; including re-underwriting every quarter for internal presentation;
* Respond to requests for portfolio level due diligence and performance updates in a timely manner;
* Work with the Brio AM global team to ensure accuracy and compliance with industry standards and maintain a deep understanding of loan documents, including covenants, terms, and legal requirements;
* Ensure all documentation is up-to-date and supports effective asset management and risk mitigation.
* Problem solving when issues arise at the loan or portfolio level and proactively identify and report credit risk, market risk, and operational risk within the portfolio, develop and implement risk mitigation strategies with Brio AM team;
* Assist in preparing and present portfolio updates, performance reports, and recommendations to internal stakeholders;
* Participate in onboarding and integration of new technology solutions to enhance portfolio monitoring and analytics;
* Establish best practices, processes, and policies for loan monitoring and reporting.

**Qualifications**
**What you should have:**

* 4+ years of experience in asset management, investment management, or financial services;
* Experience working with global or large domestic corporations, and experience in a diverse team, with responsibilities including execution of functions and tasks, improving workflows to enhance collaboration, productivity, and professional growth;
* Advanced degree in finance, business, economics, or related field;
* Strong skills in Excel and familiarity with other Microsoft Office tools;
* Exceptional communication abilities, capable of simplifying concepts;
* Proven track record of excellence in processes and workstreams in a scalable, KPI-based environment;
* Strong capabilities in both internal and external relationship management;
* Independent and collaborative working style.

